eau therefore needs CONTRACT-003 to define how explicit model constraints such as `qwen36` resolve against discovered/provider model IDs such as `Qwen-3.6-27b-MLX-8bit`.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;ROOT CAUSE WITH FILE:LINE\u0026#xA;Fizeau already has partial OpenAI-compatible provider matching in internal/provider/openai/discovery.go:135-155: it lowercases, strips the first slash prefix, and substring-matches the requested string. That is not yet the public contract, and it does not remove punctuation/special separators, so `qwen36` will not reliably match `Qwen-3.6-27b-MLX-8bit`. CONTRACT-003 currently says ModelRef concrete refs are exact at docs/helix/02-design/contracts/CONTRACT-003-fizeau-service.md:429-433, but it does not define explicit `Model` normalization/fuzzy behavior, ambiguity errors, or no-match evidence for the Execute path.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;PROPOSED FIX\u0026#xA;Amend CONTRACT-003 so Fizeau owns model constraint resolution for `ServiceExecuteRequest.Model` and `RouteRequest.Model`. The matching contract should normalize case, whitespace, and separators such as hyphen, underscore, dot, slash, colon, and other non-alphanumeric delimiters before substring matching; allow catalog aliases where present; resolve a single match to the provider/discovered canonical model ID; return a typed ambiguity error with candidates on multiple matches; and return a typed no-match error or existing provider error with nearby candidates/evidence when none match. Apply the same semantics consistently to Execute and ResolveRoute. DDx will pass raw `--model qwen36` through unchanged and record the actual model Fizeau reports.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;NON-SCOPE\u0026#xA;Do not add DDx-side normalization or matching. Do not change profile/ModelRef semantics except to clarify the difference from raw Model constraint resolution. Do not change route scoring or auto-routing eligibility except where exact/fuzzy explicit model constraints need candidate filtering. Do not make broad Levenshtein-style fuzzy guesses unless ambiguity/no-match behavior is explicitly test-covered.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;In-scope files include:\u0026#xA;- docs/helix/02-design/contracts/CONTRACT-003-fizeau-service.md\u0026#xA;- service_routing.go and routing helper packages used by Execute/ResolveRoute\u0026#xA;- internal/provider/openai/discovery.go if its matching primitive is generalized or reused\u0026#xA;- routing_errors.go if typed ambiguity/no-match errors need public shape\u0026#xA;- service_routing_errors_test.go, service_http_provider_test.go, internal/provider/openai/discovery_test.go, and public contract tests\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Out-of-scope files:\u0026#xA;- DDx repository files under ../ddx\u0026#xA;- model catalog manifest content unless adding an alias fixture is necessary for tests\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;PARENT AND DEPENDENCIES\u0026#xA;Parent: fizeau-06524f43. Dependencies: none.\n    \u003c/description\u003e\n    \u003cacceptance\u003e\n1. CONTRACT-003 states that Fizeau, not DDx, owns normalization, alias lookup, substring matching, ambiguity handling, no-match handling, and final route selection for raw `Model` constraints on Execute and ResolveRoute.\u0026#xA;2. A focused unit test proves `qwen36` matches a single model named `Qwen-3.6-27b-MLX-8bit` after separator normalization.\u0026#xA;3. A focused unit test proves case-insensitive, whitespace-insensitive, slash-prefix-tolerant matching still works for existing examples such as `qwen/qwen3.6` and `QWEN3.6`.\u0026#xA;4. A focused unit test proves ambiguous normalized substrings return a typed ambiguity error including candidate model IDs, not an arbitrary first match.\u0026#xA;5. A focused unit test proves no-match behavior preserves typed evidence for operators and does not silently fall back to an unrelated model.\u0026#xA;6. Execute and ResolveRoute use the same model constraint resolution semantics; a service-level test covers both paths.\u0026#xA;7. `go test ./... -run \u0026#34;Test.*(Model.*Fuzzy|Model.*Alias|NormalizeModel|ResolveExecuteRoute|ResolveRoute).*\u0026#34;` passes after updating exact final test names.\u0026#xA;8. `go test ./...` passes.\u0026#xA;9. `lefthook run pre-commit` passes.\n    \u003c/acceptance\u003e\n    \u003clabels\u003ephase:build, area:contract, area:routing, area:model-catalog, kind:feature, downstream:ddx\u003c/labels\u003e\n    \u003cmetadata parent=\"fizeau-06524f43\" spec-id=\"CONTRACT-003\" base-rev=\"a93d96e522060a95a0fc94170aad255f1b351a41\" bundle=\".ddx/executions/20260506T165909-a45a4243\"/\u003e\n  \u003c/bead\u003e\n  \u003cgoverning\u003e\n    \u003cref id=\"CONTRACT-003\" path=\"docs/helix/02-design/contracts/CONTRACT-003-fizeau-service.md\"\u003eCONTRACT-003: FizeauService Service Interface\u003c/ref\u003e\n  \u003c/governing\u003e\n\u003c/execute-bead\u003e\n","metadata":{"attempt_id":"20260506T165909-a45a4243","base_rev":"a93d96e522060a95a0fc94170aad255f1b351a41","bead_id":"fizeau-400b57fe","bundle_path":".ddx/executions/20260506T165909-a45a4243","correlation_id":"fizeau-400b57fe:20260506T165909-a45a4243","prompt_file":".ddx/executions/20260506T165909-a45a4243/prompt.md","prompt_sha":"5feccd7243bebaaf52ec8b2aa39bd670ce95a82fd370d74f7969426cda3ede29","role":"implementer","session_id":"eb-0063c7e6","worker_id":""}}}
